#
# Counter-example for the native math:IncompleteDependencyModel gate: a
# math:MarkovKernel declares its math:kernelDomain but is missing its
# math:kernelCodomain, so it cannot fix a stochastic transition. The native gate MUST
# emit math:IncompleteDependencyModel (and no other probability failure class).
# Back-reference: math:MarkovKernel / math:IncompleteDependencyModel (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:incompleteKernel a math:MarkovKernel ;
    math:kernelDomain ex:sourceSpace .

ex:sourceSpace a math:MeasurableSpace .
